# Private docs SSO — see wiki/private-docs.md.
#
# All three unset → auth is off; /private/** returns 404 in production builds.
#
# ── Production ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate your own secrets. Never deploy the development values below: they
# are published in this template, so anyone can read them.
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
#   DOCS_SSO_URL         your product's SSO endpoint (see the README)
#   DOCS_SSO_SECRET      signs the handoff JWT — share with your product
#   DOCS_SESSION_SECRET  signs this site's session cookie — share with nobody
#
# Deploying with the value below for DOCS_SESSION_SECRET lets anyone forge a
# session cookie with any `orgs` claim they like, which defeats every check
# this feature makes.
#
# ── Local development ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and run the mock SSO server with
# `npm run dev:sso`. These values match that server and are meant to be fake.
#
# Note they are two *different* values, deliberately. Reusing one secret for
# both is the ordinary production slip, and it would mean any token your
# product signs — an API token, a password-reset link — verifies as a docs
# session. `createSessionToken` stamps an `aud` claim to reject exactly that,
# but the habit is worth starting here.
DOCS_SSO_URL=http://localhost:4545/docs-sso
DOCS_SSO_SECRET=dev-only-sso-not-a-secret
DOCS_SESSION_SECRET=dev-only-session-not-a-secret
#
# ── Demo login (UNSAFE) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DOCS_UNSAFE_DEMO_LOGIN=1 turns /demo-login into a working sign-in that
# accepts ANYONE — a persona picker, no password. It exists for the template's
# own demo deployment and for staging sites evaluating private docs before the
# real SSO endpoint is built. On a site holding real private content it makes
# that content world-readable; the attack is spelled out in
# wiki/private-docs.md. Point DOCS_SSO_URL at this site's own /demo-login
# (absolute URL) and the ordinary round trip does the rest.
# DOCS_UNSAFE_DEMO_LOGIN=1
#
# ── Site URL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The deployed URL, used by the sitemap and llms-txt to emit absolute URLs.
# Set it here, or replace the `https://example.com` fallback in
# astro.config.mjs — they are the same setting, and this variable wins as long
# as the `DOCS_SITE_URL ||` in front of that fallback stays put. Useful when
# one build serves several environments (a preview deployment and production
# have different URLs).
# DOCS_SITE_URL=https://docs.example.com
